<title>UK: UK budget cuts spending by 2.0 billion stg - Clarke.</title>
<headline>UK budget cuts spending by 2.0 billion stg - Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said his budget cuts public spending by two billion next year and generates an extra 500 million stg of revenue.</p>
<p>Clarke said his proposals also contain &quot;a balanced tax package&quot; including tax cuts of two billion stg &quot;while it secures the tax base by 1.0 billion stg.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Taken together the effect of the budget is to tighten fiscal policy and so protect healthy lasting recovery,&quot; Clarke added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
